<task id="SRFR-042" project="set-regarding-and-field-mapping-resolver-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>RegardingResolver v1.3.4 → v1.3.5 — Row 2 hyperlink onLoad fix (pre-loaded records: derive click target from bound form fields, not just picker-selected state)</title>
    <status>completed</status>
    <estimated-effort>1h30min</estimated-effort>
    <actual-effort>~50min</actual-effort>
    <assigned>AI Agent</assigned>
    <started>2026-07-03</started>
    <completed>2026-07-03</completed>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-group>—</parallel-group>
    <tags>pcf,regarding-resolver,bug-fix,hyperlink,onload,version-bump,wave-3-followon,deploy</tags>
    <depends-on>SRFR-039</depends-on>
    <wave>3</wave>
  </metadata>

  <prompt><![CDATA[
Out-of-plan bug fix reported by owner post-v1.3.4 deploy.

Bug: Row 2 "Regarding Number" hyperlink does NOT open the target record on click
when the record was pre-loaded (existed before the user opened the form). Works
only immediately after user picks a new record via the search icon.

Root cause: `selectedTarget` React state is populated ONLY in the `onSelect`
callback. On form-load with a pre-existing regarding value, bound fields
display correctly BUT `selectedTarget` is null → click handler has no
entityName/entityId → no-op.

Fix (v1.3.5) — SIMPLE approach: derive click target on demand at click time
from Xrm.Page attributes when `selectedTarget` is null. Priority order:
  1. `selectedTarget` (fresh picker selection wins)
  2. Parse `etn` + `id` from `sprk_regardingrecordurl` attribute value
     (most robust — URL is stored on host records, contains both parts
     inline in query params `?etn=<entityLogicalName>&id=<guid>`)
  3. Fallback: `sprk_regardingrecordid` + resolve entityName from the bound
     `sprk_regardingrecordtype` lookup's entityType hint if present in
     the `(rtRef as any).entityType` extension. (Best-effort fallback if
     no URL is stored.)

The URL-parse path is the primary derivation because `sprk_regardingrecordurl`
already contains both etn and id in a well-known shape — the shared lib's
`buildRecordUrl` helper produces exactly this shape (SRFR-032 CREATE-mode
seam + shared `applyResolverFields` UPDATE-mode write).

Scope (all in `src/client/pcf/RegardingResolver/`):

1. `RegardingResolverApp.tsx`:
   - Add helper `resolveClickTarget(selectedTarget)`: reads Xrm.Page
     attributes if selectedTarget is null; returns `{ entityName, entityId }`
     or `null` if unresolvable.
   - URL parse: `new URL(recordUrl)`, extract `etn` + `id` query params.
   - Update `handleRecordNumberClick` to call the helper first, then use its
     resolved `entityName` + `entityId` for `navigateTo`.
   - Preserve all existing behavior: Xrm-unavailable → warn + no-throw;
     navigateTo rejection → catch + warn; empty-state → warn + no-op.

2. Version bump v1.3.4 → v1.3.5 across all 7 anchors:
   - `ControlManifest.Input.xml` (control root version attr)
   - `index.ts` CONTROL_VERSION
   - `RegardingResolverApp.tsx` BUILD_DATE (leave as 2026-07-03 if same day)
   - `Solution/solution.xml` <Version>
   - `Solution/Controls/sprk_Spaarke.Controls.RegardingResolver/ControlManifest.xml`
     version attr
   - `package.json` version
   - `Solution/pack.ps1` $version

3. Tests (`__tests__/RegardingResolverApp.test.tsx`):
   - Bulk grep + replace 1.3.4 → 1.3.5 (version prop + assertion regex).
   - Add 3 new tests:
     (a) Click with pre-loaded record (no selectedTarget, but Xrm.Page has
         sprk_regardingrecordurl attribute) → navigateTo called with parsed
         etn + id.
     (b) Click with fresh picker selection (selectedTarget populated) →
         navigateTo called with selection's entityType + recordId (regression
         guard — selectedTarget still wins).
     (c) Click with no selectedTarget AND no Xrm.Page attributes → warn +
         no-op (unchanged empty-state behavior).

4. Step 9.5 quality gates: `/code-review` + `/adr-check` + `npm run build:prod`.

5. Deploy: pack solution, `pac solution import --force-overwrite
   --publish-changes`, verify `pac solution list | Select-String
   RegardingResolver` shows Version 1.3.5.

Constraints:
  - ADR-022 virtual pattern preserved.
  - SRFR-034/035/037/039 features preserved: refresh button, auto-refresh,
    showVersionFooter, PolymorphicPicker consumption, Row 2 grid with labels,
    Name cell restored, title semi-bold + low top padding.
  - Backward compat: no manifest property changes; new plumbing is
    additive (reads Xrm.Page at click time, no new context bindings).
  - Xrm-unavailable path: warn + silent-continue.
  ]]></prompt>

  <role>PCF developer familiar with Spaarke PCF version discipline
  (`src/client/pcf/CLAUDE.md`), Fluent v9 Griffel + tokens (`ADR-021`),
  virtual PCF platform-library pattern (`ADR-022`), Xrm.Page/attribute
  read patterns, and defensive host-safe error handling.</role>

  <goal><![CDATA[
RegardingResolver v1.3.5 deployed to spaarkedev1, verified via
`pac solution list`. Row 2 record-number hyperlink correctly opens the
target record modal for BOTH pre-loaded records (form-load path) AND
fresh picker selections. Fix is additive — no manifest property changes,
no shared-library changes. All prior SRFR-034/035/037/039 features
preserved. All 7 version anchors bumped 1.3.4 → 1.3.5. `npm run build:prod`
passes. New tests validate the pre-loaded-record path.
  ]]></goal>

